## Calling Boxaz
- MCP: `{{.Base}}/mcp` (Streamable HTTP) or `box mcp` (stdio), header `Authorization: Bearer $BOXAZ_API_KEY`.
- REST: `{{.Base}}/v1` — e.g. `curl -X POST {{.Base}}/v1/boxes/{{.BoxID}}/exec -H "Authorization: Bearer $BOXAZ_API_KEY" -d '{"command":"ls"}'`.
- Discovery: `{{.Base}}/llms.txt`, `{{.Base}}/v1/openapi.json`, `{{.Base}}/v1/tools?format=openai`.
- Send `Accept-Language: en|vi|zh|ja` to get error messages in your language.

## Tips
- exec returns only the last 60 lines; read the full output with `box_logs(log_id)` when needed.
- Long commands: `async: true`, then `box_job(job_id, wait_s=30)`.
- Several commands: `box_exec_batch` (one round-trip).
- Snapshot before risky changes (`box_snapshot`), then `box_restore` or `box_fork` to try alternatives.
- Serving a web app: start it on 0.0.0.0:<port> in the background (`box_exec` async), then `box_url(port)` returns its public HTTPS URL.
- Delete the box with `box_down` when you are done.
